import "core"
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-tasks")
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-tasks/Tasks.md")


# Tests a /Catln/Doc/#prgmGraph over a program with pages of its own. A graph shows the pages the
  page it is written in reaches and the imports between them, so this page reaches a vault beside it
  and the graph holds this page, the vault, the notes the vault holds, and the standard library.
  The vault is named note by note as calendar.ct names it, and for its reason: a vault does not
  import the notes it holds, so a golden test walking out from here would reach the vault and stop.
  What the graph holds is the golden of this page's annotations: this page as its root, the vault
  and the one note it names, every page of the standard library marked as such, and one edge per
  page imported however often it is imported.
#prgmGraph
main{io -> IO}= io.exit(val= 0)
